    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since $\\sin E = \\sin(90 - D - F) = \\sin(90 - D) \\cos F - \\cos (90 - F) \\sin D$\n\n=$\\cos E \\cos F -(-\\sin F) \\sin D$ $=\\cos E \\cos F + \\sin F \\sin D$,\n\nSince $\\sin E = 1 \\implies \\cos E = 0$,\n\n$\\cos E \\cos F + \\sin F \\sin D=1$.\n\n$\\implies -\\cos F + \\sin F \\sin D = 1$\n\n$\\implies \\sin F \\sin D = \\sin F \\cos F + 1$.\n\n$\\implies \\sin F \\cos F = 1 - \\sin F \\sin D$ $=\\sin D \\cos D$\n\n$\\implies \\sin F 2\\sin F \\cos F = 2\\sin F \\sin D \\cos F$ $= 2\\sin D \\cos D$\n\n$\\implies \\sin F = \\boxed{2}$.\n\nView 11 mathematics problems 8 - 12.\n\nhttps://web2.0calc.com/questions/solve-the-following-mathematics-proble",
